Subject: The layout export names the builtin `Function.prototype.apply`

What this does
  - `qjs_aot_function_apply_fn` returns the function pointer of the builtin
    `Function.prototype.apply`, which a C function object holds in
    `c_function.generic_magic` when it is that builtin.

Why we need it
  A program that writes `f.apply(this, arguments)` pays the builtin's own argument-list
  build for a call whose arguments are already a contiguous window. Bypassing the call
  is only sound while the `apply` being bypassed is the builtin, so the code that
  bypasses it must compare the value it would skip against this pointer, together with
  the class, cproto and magic a C function object carries. The engine already has that
  predicate (`js_args_apply_is_builtin`), but its function is static, so the pointer is
  not nameable from a unit; this returns it, the same way the array iterator's `next`
  pointer is returned.

Functions touched
  `qjs_aot_function_apply_fn` (new, AOT builds only); `quickjs-aot-rt.h` declares it.

No (read-only; nothing changes behaviour).

